; Two fixed pads separated by open water, with a single moving platform
; ferrying between them -- the only crossing in the stage (issue #19: the
; Ferry stage). It is a waiting game: whoever is on the dock when the barge
; arrives gets to cross, so both players want to be there.
;
; The gap is what makes this stage what it is, so the numbers that hold it
; open have to be stated, not implied. PadLeft's right edge sits at x=-300
; and PadRight's left edge sits at x=300: 600 px of open water between them.
; The longest reach in the weapon roster is the staff's max_reach = 200
; (resources/staff.tres), measured from the player's own centre, so a
; player standing at a pad's very edge and fully extending that weapon
; reaches out to only 200 px past the edge -- 400 px short of the far pad.
; 600 px is a 3x margin over that 200 px reach, not a near thing, and there
; is nothing solid out over the water to plant a swing on in the first
; place unless the barge happens to be under it.
;
; The barge (MovingPlatform, issue #18) is 160 px wide, authored at
; x=-220 and travelling 440 px right to x=220, both at the pads' shared
; y=380. At the near end its left edge (-220-80=-300) sits exactly on
; PadLeft's right edge; at the far end its right edge (220+80=300) sits
; exactly on PadRight's left edge. Flush both ways, so docking is a step,
; not a jump, at either end. 4 s a leg (110 px/s) is slow enough that
; reaching the dock before it arrives is a real wait rather than a
; formality, and fast enough that a round is not spent mostly standing
; still.

